1
00:00:00,876 --> 00:00:03,826
(Sheldon:)My quantum gravity's
positively Ioopy!

2
00:00:05,381 --> 00:00:06,981
(Penny:)Who's the duchess?

3
00:00:07,149 --> 00:00:08,929
(Leonard:)One of the people
that lives in his head.

4
00:00:10,519 --> 00:00:13,059
(Amy:)I hope he's this distraught
if he ever breaks up with me.

5
00:00:13,222 --> 00:00:15,862
(Leonard:)Well, if he does, I'll see
if my bear has a friend.

6
00:00:18,494 --> 00:00:20,994
(Penny:)Sheldon, have you ever considered
not rushing into something new?

7
00:00:21,163 --> 00:00:23,663
(Penny:)I mean, why don't you
take your time, enjoy your freedom?

8
00:00:23,832 --> 00:00:26,872
(Penny:)Maybe something new
to study will find you.

9
00:00:28,103 --> 00:00:30,053
(Sheldon:)That's actually not bad advice.

10
00:00:30,206 --> 00:00:32,686
(Sheldon:)You know, I didn't seek out
string theory.

11
00:00:32,775 --> 00:00:35,255
(Sheldon:)It just hit me
over the head one day.

12
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:36,551
(Amy:)How does that happen?

13
00:00:36,712 --> 00:00:38,952
(Sheldon:)A bully chased me through
the school library

14
00:00:39,114 --> 00:00:41,894
(Sheldon:)and hit me over the head with
the biggest book he could find.

15
00:00:43,385 --> 00:00:45,865
OK, how about we toast
your new-found freedom?

16
00:00:47,022 --> 00:00:49,232
(Sheldon:)Normally I refrain from alcohol,

17
00:00:49,391 --> 00:00:52,431
(Sheldon:)but since my cerebral cortex is
twiddling its proverbial thumbs,

18
00:00:52,595 --> 00:00:54,305
(Sheldon:)why not soak it in grape juice

19
00:00:54,463 --> 00:00:56,773
(Sheldon:)that's been predigested
by a fungus?

20
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,020
(Penny:)And you wonder why other
children beat you with books.

